# The story with another player character (wish of the project owner, 03.11.2026: the cheat menu's section
# "Player character"; runtime/cheats.cpp, port/docs/cheat-menu-plan.md). The game itself can play every room with
# Ada, HUNK, Krauser or Wesker (its debug start menu picks pl_type), but outside their own games their tables
# end with their Mercenaries weapons and their archives lack Leon's story props; the events, the radio screen
# and the room items assume Leon. With this patch a stand-in plays the story as Leon would:
# - game.cpp gameRoomInit: before the player data is read, re4_story_char_room sets the type the cheat wants
#   (Leon becomes the character, the character Leon again when the cheat is off; Ashley's part stays hers);
#   cGameSave::save writes Leon (pl_type 0, his costume) into every save made with a stand-in.
# - read.cpp ReadWepData: a weapon of Leon's the character has no file of its own for (every one but the knife,
#   the grenades and its Mercenaries weapons) is read from Leon's table, with bit 0x80 in oldWepId (Wesker's
#   numbers 4 and 5 are his grenades and rifle); Krauser's own buffer when gameInit made none.
# - event.cpp, obj18.cpp: the events get Leon's body and cloth from Leon's archive (read by the cheat into the
#   development half of MEM1), as their motions and parts are Leon's; without it the body was missing
#   ("Event::ExePacket_SetOm : dat failed").
# - pl_sub.cpp: HUNK, Krauser and Wesker keep Leon's costume rule (the events' parts, the vest), PlIsArmor
#   protects them as it would Leon.
# - sce_at.cpp: the room items for Leon (player_type 1: the story's keys, ammo, treasure) and the system items
#   as for Leon; with mask 2 every Leon item of the room was missing.
# - Sscrn/ss_model.cpp: the case screen shows the character as with its knife while a weapon of Leon's is armed
#   (its knife file; the name was left unset, the empty weapon model's light logged "litHitCk PNo0"), the radio
#   screen shows Leon from his archive.
# - pl06.cpp, pl0d/pl_wesker.cpp, pl02.cpp setLeftHand: Leon's weapons ask for left hands 2..5 (fore-end, TMP grip,
#   handgun support, mine thrower) the characters partly lack; a missing number was taken as a model pointer
#   (HUNK with Leon's handgun crashed in cModInfoMgr::create): the nearest hand of the character; Leon's hand 5
#   that his Striker passes as a pointer into the player archive (pl0a/pl_klauser.cpp as well).
# Not a bug of the prototype: a port feature (the cheat menu). Without a stand-in nothing changes.
